Package: sfa
Version: 1.2.1
Date: 2026-09-07
Title: Stochastic Frontier Analysis
Type: Package
Authors@R: c(person("David", "Bernstein",
                     email = "davebernstein1@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                     comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2267-5741")),
              person("Christopher", "Parmeter", role = c("aut")),
              person("Alexander", "Stead", role = c("aut")))
Maintainer: David Bernstein <davebernstein1@gmail.com>
Description: Maximum likelihood estimation of stochastic frontier models, in
    which observed output falls short of an unobserved production frontier by a
    one-sided inefficiency term in addition to symmetric noise, following
    Aigner, Lovell and Schmidt (1977) <doi:10.1016/0304-4076(77)90052-5> and
    Meeusen and van den Broeck (1977) <doi:10.2307/2525757>. Cross-sectional
    models cover fifteen noise and inefficiency distribution pairs, with
    heteroskedasticity permitted in either error component. Panel models
    include the true fixed and random effects estimators of Greene (2005)
    <doi:10.1016/j.jeconom.2004.05.003> and the four-component model of
    Colombi, Kumbhakar, Martini and Vittadini (2014)
    <doi:10.1007/s11123-014-0386-y>. Further entry points address zero
    inefficiency, latent classes, two-tier frontiers, sample selection,
    nonparametric frontiers, dependence between the error components, and
    endogenous regressors after Amsler, Prokhorov and Schmidt (2016)
    <doi:10.1016/j.jeconom.2015.06.013>. Technical efficiency prediction,
    marginal effects, and specification tests for wrong skewness, for the
    assumed inefficiency distribution and for heteroskedasticity are provided.
